<sect> mat3 (Revision 1.1 -- 22/04/98)

<p>The unit <tt/mat3/ regroups routines for vector and matrix operations
in three dimensional space.

<sect1>Vector operations

<sect2>v3_copy
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int v3_copy (const double a[3], double b[3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p> Copy of vector <tt/a/ to vector <tt/b/.

<sect2>v3_add
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int v3_add (const double a[3], const double b[3], double c[3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Vector addition (<tt/c = a + b/).

<sect2>v3_sub
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int v3_sub (const double a[3], const double b[3], double c[3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Vector substraction (<tt/c = a - b/).

<sect2>v3_multx
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int v3_multx (const double a[3], const double x, double c[3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p> Multiplication of a vector with a scalar. (<tt/c = x*a/)

<sect2>v3_norm
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int v3_norm (const double a[3], double c[3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Normation of a vector (<tt/c =norm(a)/)

<sect2>v3_length
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
double v3_length (const double a[3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Return value is the length of the vector <tt/a/.

<sect2>v3_scalar
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
double v3_scalar (const double a[3], const double b[3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p> Return value is the scalar product of vector <tt/a/ and vector <tt/b/.

<sect2>v3_cross
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int v3_cross (const double a[3], const double b[3], double c[3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Cross product of 2 vectors. (<tt/c = a x b/).


<sect1>Matrix operations

<sect2>m3_unit
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int m3_unit (double a[3][3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p> Filling of  matrix <tt/m/ as unit matrix. (<tt/1/ on diagonal <tt/0/ elsewhere).

<sect2>m3_copy
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int m3_copy (const double a[3][3], double c[3][3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p> Copy of matrix <tt/a/ to matrix <tt/c/.

<sect2>m3_trans
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int m3_trans (const double a[3][3], double c[3][3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Transposition of  matrix (<tt/c = a(transposed)/).

<sect2>m3_write
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
void m3_write (FILE *fpout, const double a[3][3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Writes matrix <tt/a/ to file <tt/fpout/.

<sect2> m3_add
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int m3_add (const double a[3][3], const double b[3][3], double c[3][3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p> Matrix addition (<tt/c =  a + b/).

<sect2> m3_sub
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int m3_sub (const double a[3][3], const double b[3][3], double c[3][3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Matrix substraction (<tt/c =  a - b/).

<sect2>m3v3_mult
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int m3v3_mult (const double a[3][3], const double b[3], double c[3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Multiplication of a matrix with a vector. (<tt/c = a * b/).

<sect2>m3m3_mult
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int m3m3_mult (const double a[3][3], const double b[3][3], double c[3][3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Multiplication of a matrix with a matrix. (<tt/c = a * b/).

<sect2>m3_inv
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int m3_inv (double a[3][3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p> Inversion of a matrix. Matrix <tt/m/ is overwritten by its
inverse. A return value different from <tt/0/ indicates failure of inversion.


<sect1>Rotation matrices

<p>In all following routines rotations are considered to be right hand 
rotations of the reference frame. The approach here is that physically a vector 
is considered to remain unchanged, only the decomposition of this vector changes 
when the coordinate frame is rotated. (Note that if you prefer to look at rotations
as rotations of a moving vector with respect to a  fixed reference frame than 
all routines are dealing with left hand rotations).

<sect2>rot_getmat
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int rot_getmat (const int axis, const double angle, double rotmat[3][3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>This function determines the rotation matrix <tt/rotmat/ given the rotation
axis <tt/axis/ (1 = rotation around x, 2 =  rotation around y, 3 = rotation 
around z) and the rotation angle <tt/angle/ in radian.

<sect2>rotate
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int rotate (const double x1[3], const int axis, const double angle, double x2[3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>This function performs a rotation of a vector <tt/x1/ around the axis <tt/axis/
 (1 = rotation around x, 2 =  rotation around y, 3 = rotation around z). The rotation
angle <tt/angle/ is given in radian. Result vector is <tt/x2/. Here an example : 
<tscreen><verb> 
  input     x1=(1, 0, 0) 
  rotation  rotate (x1, 3, PI/2, x2)
  output    x2=(0,-1, 0)
</verb></tscreen>

<sect2>rotvec_to_mat
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int rotvec_to_mat (const double rotvec[3], const double angle, double rotmat[3][3])
</verb></tscreen>
<p>this function determines the rotation matrix <tt/rotmat/ given the rotation
axis as a unit vector <tt/rotvec/ and the rotation angle <tt/angle/ in radians.

<sect2>rotmat_to_vec
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int rotmat_to_vec (const double rotmat[3][3], double rotvec[3], double *angle)
</verb></tscreen>
<p>this function determines the rotation vector <tt/rotmat/ given the rotation
axis as a unit vector <tt/rotvec/ and the rotation angle <tt/angle/ in radians.
